# 24-hour time

All times shown in the UI, PDFs, emails, and exports use **24-hour** clock (`HH:mm`). Never use 12-hour time or AM/PM.

## Do

- Format times with helpers from `@/lib/dates`: `formatTime`, `formatDateTime`, `formatTimestamp`
- Collect times with `TimeInput` from `@/components/ui/TimeInput` (text `HH:mm`)
- Prefer `hourCycle: "h23"` / `hour12: false` if calling `Intl.DateTimeFormat` directly

## Don't

```ts
// ❌ BAD — native time inputs follow the OS locale and often show AM/PM
<input type="time" />
date.toLocaleTimeString()
date.toLocaleString()
new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", { hour: "numeric", minute: "numeric" })

// ✅ GOOD
import { TimeInput } from "@/components/ui/TimeInput";
<TimeInput name="startTime" defaultValue="13:30" />
formatTime("14:30")
formatDateTime(iso)
new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", { hour: "2-digit", minute: "2-digit", hourCycle: "h23" })
```

Examples: `08:00`, `13:30`, `23:59` — not `8:00 AM` / `1:30 PM`.
